--- !u!114 &1789635226
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1789635225}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: e7e54b51643c866409c375da6fc9c651, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  lookSensitivity: 1
  moveSensitivity: 1
  worldLimits: {x: 300, y: 100, z: 300}
  slowMotionFactor: 0.2
  slowMotionLerpDuration: 1
  terrain: {fileID: 248842810}
  infoText: '<b><size=20>THOR_<i>Thunderstorm</i></size></b>


    <b>Lightning fast</b><color=#c9c9c9ff>
    - Every aspect is as optimized as possible. Low overdraw, usage of only one spotlight(optional),
    usage of very few audiosources, only one texture atlas for lightning bolts, simple
    but powerful shaders and automatic pooling. Compatibility issues with other assets
    are avoided.</color>

    <b>Easy to use</b><color=#c9c9c9ff> - Drag and drop
    the prefab into your scene and you are ready to go. The API is as simple as it
    can be and the code is well commented. Every property in the handy custom inspector
    has tooltips.</color>

    <b>Sounds great</b><color=#c9c9c9ff> - The 30 included
    samples are carefully recorded and edited with game audio in mind from the get
    go. Rain noise has been minimized during recording and carefully filtered out
    in editing. What you get is pure thunder and lightning ready for integration
    in your weather system.</color>

    <b>Looks fantastic</b><color=#c9c9c9ff>
    - Even in slow motion. High speed video footage of lightning strikes was the
    reference. The scripts, shaders, textures and meshes were created to work well
    together for a truly immersive thunderstorm experience.</color>


    <b>THOR_<i>Thunderstorm</i></b><color=#c9c9c9ff>
    is used in D.R.O.N.E.</color> <color=#68aefdff>www.dronethegame.com</color>'
  controlsText: '<b>Controls:</b>

    Drag the "Lightning Probability" slider to
    the right to start the thunder storm.

    Hold the right mouse button to look
    and move (WASD, QE, Shift).

    Press the space bar to enable/disable slow motion.

    To
    evaluate the performance, click the "Hide Terrain" button.

    For more Information
    click the "Show Info" button.'
